body:
Here's a proposed implementation that will add the possibility of specifying an array of intially selected items to the useGroupModel composable.

This implementation adds a `selected` property to the `useGroupModel` config object. The property accepts a function whose first parameter is an array of options which comes from the `options` property on the config object. The function can then be used to return an array values to be selected by default.

This will be a good feature to have as it comes in handy in so many use cases. Take for instance, you have a list of selected fruits stored somewhere and you want them to be selected by default on the group model.

With the above scenario, here's the proposed implementation

```ts
const alreadySelected = ["apple", "banana"]
const { options, select, value } = useGroupModel<string>({
  options: ['apple', 'banana', 'orange', 'watermelon'],
  multi: true,
  selected: (options: string[]) => {
    const select = []
    options.forEach(opt => {
      if (alreadySelected.includes(opt))
        select.push(opt)
    })

    return select
  },
})

console.log(value) // ["apple", "banana"]
```

This PR also helps improve some logic in a few places such as what is returned in the `value` property. It now returns an plain array if multiple options is selected or a single option. This is to me should be the expected result rather than a `Set`.

This PR also fixed the type definition of the `value` of the value property as returned by the composable which initially didn't match-up with the logic. It is expected to return a `ref` wrapping a value but was returning a plain value.

Please review. Thanks 🙏

